# LocateAnything Docker

Build the reusable serving image once:

```bash
docker build -t locateanything-openai:3b /data0/work/LuoWeiXing/LocateAnything
```

If `vllm/vllm-openai:v0.13.0` already exists locally, it can also be used as
the base image:

```bash
docker build \
  --build-arg BASE_IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai:v0.13.0 \
  -t locateanything-openai:3b \
  /data0/work/LuoWeiXing/LocateAnything
```

Start a server. Users usually only need to change `--name`, `--gpus`, `-p`,
`-v`, and `SERVED_MODEL_NAME`.

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name locateanything-3b \
  --gpus '"device=0"' \
  --shm-size 16g \
  -p 8010:8000 \
  -v /data0/work/LuoWeiXing/LocateAnything:/model:ro \
  -e SERVED_MODEL_NAME=locateanything-3b \
  -e MODEL_PATH=/model \
  -e DEVICE=cuda \
  -e DTYPE=bfloat16 \
  -e GENERATION_MODE=hybrid \
  -e MAX_NEW_TOKENS=8192 \
  locateanything-openai:3b
```

Stop and remove:

```bash
docker stop locateanything-3b && docker rm locateanything-3b
```

Health check:

```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8010/health
```

Multipart prediction:

```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8010/predict \
  -F image=@example.jpg \
  -F task=ground_multi \
  -F text='people wearing red shirts'
```

OpenAI-style multimodal call:

```bash
IMAGE_B64=$(base64 -w 0 example.jpg)
curl http://127.0.0.1:8010/v1/chat/completions \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{
    "model": "locateanything-3b",
    "messages": [{
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
        {"type": "text", "text": "Locate all the instances that match the following description: person."},
        {"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "data:image/jpeg;base64,'"$IMAGE_B64"'"}}
      ]
    }]
  }'
```
